      "mergedPostDetails": "\"OK\" button in world loading space was becoming far away from me and finally unreachable to push except I use playspace mover on VR mode. This phenomenon is observed in open-beta version that carrying out at 2022-07-30. \nThe world loading space where I say is the space shown on our moving between one instance to another instance. In this space, we wait world downloading and finally push \"OK\" to move another instance, right?\nHowever, that \"OK\" button location is becoming far away and inconvenient direction from my head in this open-beta. \n(In exactly, \"OK\" button and other UI Elements: information and the button to move home, world were also placed on same inconvenient coordinates) \nI guess the distance and direction that shown \"OK\" relate with player's head angle and horizon that their set from wing menu. On the case that the first joining to home world instance (the operation on log in), this phenomenon is not caused.\nIf this phenomenon has not been fixed until official release of next version, I would be a great \"OK\" button sniper. :)\nMy Playing Environment: Quest2 + VirtualDesktop (SteamVR) and sitting on chair.",
